  "description": "Extension of existing dwelling and development of property to create a more useable, productive, and sustainable home for a growing family.\n\nThere will be a full removal of the existing rear chimney breast in order to make room for the loft conversion and to add a small extra square meterage to an existing bedroom and reception room. The chimney breast to the front of the house will be extended above the new roofline so that it remains useable with the loft extension. The existing bathroom will be made smaller in order to lengthen the staircase and make it shallower. The existing southernmost bedroom will give way to a landing for a staircase leading to the loft conversion.\n\nA basement will be dug in the side return and to the rear underneath the new extension and rear patio. This area is to house utilities for the home (including but not limited to solar controllers, grey water recycling, and rain water catchment for non-potable and garden uses), storage, a full bathroom, and second reception area.\n\nOn the ground floor, the existing kitchen will be split into additional storage and a pantry for the new kitchen. The side extension will contain a laundry/mudroom, toilet, and small workshop/storage. To the rear will contain the new kitchen/breakfast room.\n\nOn the first floor, the 2 remaining bedrooms will be made slightly smaller in order to open a hallway between them leading to the side extension which will contain an additional bedroom and bathroom for this level and closets for each of the 3 bedrooms on this level.\n\nThe loft conversion will have a max hight aligning with the existing roof line. It will contain a master suite with 2 closets and an on-suite bathroom in the side extension with 1 closet.\n\nAll materials on the outer facades are to match the existing.\n\nIn totality, the house is going from 3 bed, 1 bath, and 1 reception to 4 bed, 4.5 bath, and 2 receptions.\n\nThe rear garden is a steeply sloping area that will be cleared and subtly terraced in order make the space more useable and productive. There will be a covered patio with outdoor kitchen/food prep area and outdoor seating contained by a retaining wall. This area will also house compressors for air conditioning/air source heat pumps that will service throughout the house, replacing the existing gas boiler and providing summer cooling.\n\nThe rest of the garden will be developed into a permaculture space for growing food, small animals, and a wildlife and pollinator friendly space with native flora and fauna and pond. A greenhouse made from recycled materials will be erected in the middle of the property and will fall under permitted development. To the rear/top there will be two additional out structures that also fall within permitted development, one to house chickens, and the other a bathroom (on house water and waste systems), office, and mini-barn.\n\nOn top of the house and out structures, there will be solar panels for renewable energy generation.\n",
